## B5 — trio-leak pin e2e fixture.
##
## Source: docs/specs/system/zero_rust_stdlib_classes.spec.md.
##
## Exercises every auto-connect path a fresh stdlib package should
## reach without compiler edits beyond a single BOOTSTRAP_FILES entry:
##   1. User-body `def init` + `def get` resolved through the
##      bootstrap pass-2 walk (B1).
##   2. Module-scope `lib "..."` free fn + a pure-Riven helper that
##      calls it.
##   3. `def drop as "riven_foobar_drop"(self)` class-body lib decl
##      that fires through drop-elaboration (B4 + B1).
##
## Send / Sync auto-derive (B2) is asserted by the
## `compiler/riven_core/tests/trio_leak_pin.rs` Rust pin (it queries
## `Ty::is_send_strict_with` directly); the e2e binary cannot observe
## auto-trait satisfiability at runtime.

def main
  let x = FooBar.new(42)
  let v = x.get
  let doubled = foobar_double_plus_one(20)
  if v == 42
    if doubled == 41
      puts "ok"
    else
      puts "fail-doubled"
    end
  else
    puts "fail-get"
  end
end
